== Trivia ==
* It is the posthumous version of {{e|Polycephalus}}. It appears that the top heads have been stripped of their skin, while the bottom head only lacks its first skin layer.
** Unlike its alive counterpart, the lower head has closed eyes and eyelids.
** As of Repentance, the Stain is more common in terms of floor variants than Polycephalus, since it can appear in the {{s|Caves}} and the {{s|Flooded Caves}}, whereas Polycephalus can only appear in the {{s|Catacombs}}. This means that the player is more likely to encounter the Stain than Polycephalus, despite the Stain being a posthumous version of it.
* The Stain has an alternative more degraded variation known as {{e|The Pile}}.
* A third head can be seen in the background in The Stain's boss art.
* {{dlc|na+}} Prior to [[Booster Packs#Booster Pack #5|Booster Pack #5]], The Stain could spawn {{e|Drowned Charger}}s if it was fought in the {{s|Flooded Caves}}.
* During the versus screen, The Stain's popping out sound can be heard. The Stain is one of {{Dlc|nr}} seven/{{Dlc|r}} five bosses that can be heard in the versus screen; the other are {{e|The Forsaken}}, {{e|Big Horn}}, {{e|Mom}}, {{Dlc|nr}} {{e|Mom's Heart}}, {{Dlc|nr}} {{e|It Lives!}}, and {{e|Mother}}.

